  --uom: string # Specifies the units to measure usage. **Character limit**: 25 **Values**: a configured unit of measure **Note**: You must specify this field when creating the following charge models: - Per Unit Pricing - Volume Pricing - Overage Pricing - Tiered Pricing - Tiered with Overage Pricing
  --up-to-periods: int # Specifies the length of the period during which the charge is active. If this period ends before the subscription ends, the charge ends when this period ends. **Character limit**: 5 **Values**: a whole number between 0 and 65535, exclusive **Note**: - You must use this field together with the `UpToPeriodsType` field to specify the time period. This field is applicable only when the `EndDateCondition` field is set to `FixedPeriod`. - If the subscription end date is subsequently changed through a Renewal, or Terms and Conditions amendment, the charge end date will change accordingly up to the original period end. (format: int64)
